{"title":"Factorions","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><p><b>Factorions</b> are numbers such that the sum of the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Factorial\" title=\"Factorial\">factorials</a> of its digits is equal to the number itself.\n</p><p>There only exists <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> factorions in <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Base_10\" title=\"Base 10\">Base 10</a>. They are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/a/d/4ad5e9840d7d116739b10ac1708d74eea2561bcb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1,2,145,40585$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"117\" height=\"17\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/0/5704a6bd9c2f670b45dabc70e2e5cf93dc742161.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1!=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"46\" height=\"13\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/6/3/46377b53287d0b7f76190da9e05acbd0fdedd334.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2!=2$\" width=\"47\" height=\"13\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/2/a/92a8b5fcd02fd8a45dbb64ea68509950ccbb6dcb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1!+4!+5!=1+24+120=145$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"263\" height=\"16\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/0/4/2040582419c6b3f6fc9be8268fa293c878a6b20c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4!+0!+5!+8!+5!=24+1+120+40320+120=40585$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"472\" height=\"16\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Factorions&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Factorial\" title=\"Factorial\">Factorial</a></li></ul>\n<p><i>This article is a stub.  Help us out by <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=Factorions&amp;action=edit\">expanding it</a></span>.</i>\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018084413\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.012 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.016 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 41/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 271/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 4/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 1076/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    7.218      1 Template:Stub\n100.00%    7.218      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:37307:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018084413 and revision id 287989. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}